<%# The standing band: where you stand this period, in one sentence.
    Local: `presenter` (HomePresenter). See the UI design spec §4.1. %>
<div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded p-6">
  <% if presenter.covered? %>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">You're covered this period</h2>
    <%# `presenter.buffer`, not `available - total_required`: an account-less pool counts in
        the requirement and can never be funded, so the subtraction prints a negative buffer
        at a user whose accounts are perfectly in order. %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      <%= number_to_currency(presenter.buffer) %> stays in your buffer.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-status-danger">
      <%= number_to_currency(presenter.shortfall) %> short this period
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      You need <strong><%= number_to_currency(presenter.total_required) %></strong> to stay on schedule.
      You have <strong><%= number_to_currency(presenter.available) %></strong>.
    </p>

    <%# Whenever the two figures above cannot be subtracted to reach the headline. There are
        exactly two reasons (see HomePresenter#shortfall), and each says its own half: cash in
        an account whose pools are already funded, and money owed by a pool no account can
        fund. Gating on the buffer alone stayed silent on the second — which is the ordinary
        screen for a single account with a savings goal. Silent when neither applies, since a
        consequence is only worth stating when there is one (principle 3). %>
    <% if presenter.buffer.positive? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <%= number_to_currency(presenter.buffer) %> of that sits in accounts with nothing left
        to fund, so it can't close the gap — the shortfall is what your pools miss, account by account.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <% if presenter.orphan_pools.any? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <%= number_to_currency(presenter.orphan_required) %> of what you need belongs to
        <%= pluralize(presenter.orphan_pools.size, "pool") %> with no account, listed below.
        Money can't close that — giving it an account can.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%# An overdraft is money already spent, so it is neither part of #available nor part of
      #shortfall. It has to be said here or the figures above read as the whole truth. %>
  <% presenter.overdrawn_accounts.each do |account| %>
    <p class="mt-4 rounded bg-status-danger-light px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-status-danger">
      <%= account.name %> is <%= pool_status_label(presenter.status_for(account)) %> — already spent,
      and none of the figures above count it.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# Deliberately a dead link: the sacrifice view that answers this is Plan 2c. %>
  <% if presenter.structurally_underwater? %>
    <%= link_to("Your budget doesn't fit your income",
                "#",
                class: "mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border " \
                       "border-status-danger text-status-danger text-sm font-medium") %>
  <% end %>
</div>
